  "notes": "Verified 1920 modern scholarly Work jointly associated with Morris Jastrow, Jr. and Albert T. Clay. It presents two Old Babylonian tablet fragments, transliteration, translation, commentary, and plates. It is distinct from the provisional ancient Old Babylonian Gilgamesh tradition, the Penn and Yale physical tablets, later eBL/CDLI composites, the Standard Babylonian poem, and every later edition or translation. No source text or philological reading is accepted by this record.",
